From 73d76250fbcbc4184bddd1ae9a8c2609186036a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SmartDesk Admin Feature <dev@smartdesk.ai>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:35:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Super Admin tenant management: create, edit, link owners,
 platform overview

Implements the Super Admin -> Tenants workflow using ONLY existing
architecture -- no new authentication system, no Supabase service-role
key, no invitation emails (explicitly deferred per instructions).

Database:
- Tenant model gains plan, owner_name, owner_email, owner_phone -- these
  were declared nowhere before this change; confirmed absent both in the
  committed code (git show HEAD) and on the live Supabase database
  (information_schema query) before adding them.
- Migration 0004_tenant_admin_fields: idempotent (IF NOT EXISTS) column
  and constraint creation, verified via up/down/up against a real,
  locally-installed Postgres 16 instance, not just SQLite.
- No new table. Owner 'linked' status is derived entirely from whether a
  Membership(tenant_id, role='owner') row exists -- reusing the exact
  mechanism the CLI 'flask grant' command already used, not a second one.

Backend (smartdesk/api/admin_api.py, new blueprint, require_platform_admin
on every route):
- GET/POST /api/v1/admin/tenants -- list all tenants with computed
  receptionist/channel/owner-link status; create a tenant + receptionist
  profile + blank knowledge sections + automation placeholders, exactly
  matching the existing seed pattern, never inventing business facts.
- GET/PATCH /api/v1/admin/tenants/<id> -- detail view; edit fields
  including status (activate/deactivate) and plan.
- POST /api/v1/admin/tenants/<id>/owner -- links an EXISTING Supabase-
  authenticated user (found by email in the users table) as tenant owner.
  404s with a clear message if they haven't signed up yet -- never a
  crash. Idempotent on re-link; updates rather than duplicates an
  existing membership row.
- GET /api/v1/admin/overview -- real, database-derived platform totals
  (tenants, active/inactive, active receptionists, connected channels,
  total conversations). No demo numbers.

Frontend (frontend/src/pages/AdminTenants.jsx, new):
- Tenants list page: platform stats cards, tenant table (business/owner/
  receptionist/channel/status/created/Open Dashboard), Create Tenant form.
- Tenant detail page: edit business info, activate/deactivate, Link
  Owner form, Open Dashboard button (reuses the existing tenant switcher
  -- does not duplicate it).
- Sidebar gets a 'Tenants' nav item, visible only when
  user.is_platform_admin -- both as a UX nicety AND backed by a
  RequirePlatformAdmin route guard, though the real enforcement is
  server-side (confirmed by tests, not just intended).

Tests (tests/test_admin_tenants.py, 27 new): every explicit scenario from
the request -- Tenant A cannot create/edit tenants, cannot link owners,
cannot access platform stats; Platform Admin can do all of the above; a
newly linked owner can reach only their own tenant, proven end-to-end
through the real Membership/RBAC chain, not asserted in isolation.

Full suite: 235/235 passing (was 208 before this change).
